Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version ^2.0.1) using npm
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Code Integration
Modified: web/app/layout.tsx
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` section in the RootLayout component

### 3. Implementation Details
The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Project uses Next.js App Router (confirmed by presence of app/layout.tsx)
- Analytics component is added to the root layout for site-wide tracking
- Component is placed at the end of the body element, following best practices

### 4. Verification
All checks passed successfully:
✓ TypeScript type checking (npm run typecheck) - no errors
✓ Next.js production build (npm run build) - compiled successfully
✓ Test suite (npm run test) - all 75 tests passed across 7 test files

## Notes
- The Analytics component will automatically inject tracking scripts into the application
- After deployment to Vercel, analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
- The component adds routes scoped at `/_vercel/insights/*` for tracking
- No additional configuration is required; the component works out of the box with Vercel deployments
